  "description": "This page includes an overview of the spring course and a list of all the badges and microcredentials required to earn the course credential.",
  "image": "public/b61f04c-Purple Overview.png",
  "html": "<p><b>Welcome to the Sustaining Literacy Routines Online Modules, </b>designed to support teachers participating in their first year of the Missouri's Literacy th@t Works professional learning opportunity. ​</p><a data-type=\"image-upload\" data-file-id=\"d10eb8ae-3a6c-49d1-b7de-ae0b71276cdb\" data-width=\"68.45238095238095\" class=\"self-center w-full\"><img src=\"https://participate.community/img/k/public/59aeb5e-image.png\" class=\"w-full\"></a><p></p><p>Each year of the Literacy th@t Works program combines in-person meetings with flexible online modules that support teachers in deepening their understanding of literacy practices. Just like in the fall, in the spring you will complete four modules, including a “teacher as researcher” module where you will try out a 3-4 day lesson sequence in your classroom, gather evidence, and share insights from your experience with other teachers in our learning community.</p><p>This online space is designed to help you deepen your understanding of routine literacy practices while also receiving targeted support from an online course facilitator, who will help you consider the implications for your specific students and teaching context.</p><h2 class=\"text-4xl font-bold\" data-version=\"0\" id=\"h_-spring-modules-overview\">📋 Spring Modules Overview</h2><p>During the spring online course modules, we will build on your experiences in the fall semester of Literacy th@t Works. This spring course builds on the foundations established in <i>Cultivating Literacy Routines</i> by deepening teachers’ use of writing, reading, and inquiry routines in the classroom. Through four connected modules, you will explore ways to sustain daily and weekly writing practices, support students in joining conversations across multiple texts, layer reading and writing to develop perspective, and engage in teacher-research to reflect on and share your learning. Each module is designed to involve approximately 1-2 hours of self-paced coursework. The course is organized in this way to support your planning for completing the spring modules between now and April 8th, 2026.</p><p>You have access to all of the modules, so feel free to work at a pace that works best for you and your schedule!</p><h3 class=\"text-2xl font-semibold\" id=\"h_sustaining-literacy-routines-modules\">Sustaining Literacy Routines Modules</h3><div data-type=\"doc-embed\" data-doc-id=\"adebdcd4-d3c9-439b-bb5f-88cfd9a1b9df\" data-doc-type=\"module\"><a href=\"https://participate.community/docs/adebdcd4-d3c9-439b-bb5f-88cfd9a1b9df\" class=\"flex flex-col border border-slate-300\"><div class=\"font-bold bg-slate-300 h-6 w-full pl-4\">Module</div><div class=\"flex justify-between\"><div class=\"p-4 flex flex-col justify-between\"><p class=\"font-bold line-clamp-1\">Everyday Sparks 2.0: Deepening Routine Writing</p><p class=\"text-slate-600 line-clamp-2\">Building on the Everyday Sparks work from the fall, this module invites teachers to explore strategies for sustaining routine writing throughout the year while deepening students’ thinking and engagement.</p><p class=\"text-slate-400 text-sm\">participate.community</p></div><img class=\"h-32 w-32 border-l border-slate-300 object-cover\" src=\"https://participate.community/img/k/public/9c5e059-Pink%20Module%201.png\"></div></a></div><div data-type=\"doc-embed\" data-doc-id=\"d995fa13-993f-4d3d-a0d5-63c3623a8b8e\" data-doc-type=\"module\"><a href=\"https://participate.community/docs/d995fa13-993f-4d3d-a0d5-63c3623a8b8e\" class=\"flex flex-col border border-slate-300\"><div class=\"font-bold bg-slate-300 h-6 w-full pl-4\">Module</div><div class=\"flex justify-between\"><div class=\"p-4 flex flex-col justify-between\"><p class=\"font-bold line-clamp-1\">Reading to Write: Joining a Conversation</p><p class=\"text-slate-600 line-clamp-2\">This module explores argument as conversation by introducing strategies that help students read across texts and engage with multiple perspectives.</p><p class=\"text-slate-400 text-sm\">participate.community</p></div><img class=\"h-32 w-32 border-l border-slate-300 object-cover\" src=\"https://participate.community/img/k/public/8aed571-Pink%20Module%202.png\"></div></a></div><div data-type=\"doc-embed\" data-doc-id=\"a9ac5911-3c0c-48e2-ac8d-ae33e902512e\" data-doc-type=\"module\"><a href=\"https://participate.community/docs/a9ac5911-3c0c-48e2-ac8d-ae33e902512e\" class=\"flex flex-col border border-slate-300\"><div class=\"font-bold bg-slate-300 h-6 w-full pl-4\">Module</div><div class=\"flex justify-between\"><div class=\"p-4 flex flex-col justify-between\"><p class=\"font-bold line-clamp-1\">Layering Reading, Writing, and Discussion</p><p class=\"text-slate-600 line-clamp-2\">This module explores how layering reading, writing, and discussion helps students engage with multiple full-length texts, track evolving thinking, and develop informed claims.</p><p class=\"text-slate-400 text-sm\">participate.community</p></div><img class=\"h-32 w-32 border-l border-slate-300 object-cover\" src=\"https://participate.community/img/k/public/c7671ec-Pink%20Module%203.png\"></div></a></div><div data-type=\"doc-embed\" data-doc-id=\"63533ecf-0795-4660-99b2-e55235e51946\" data-doc-type=\"module\"><a href=\"https://participate.community/docs/63533ecf-0795-4660-99b2-e55235e51946\" class=\"flex flex-col border border-slate-300\"><div class=\"font-bold bg-slate-300 h-6 w-full pl-4\">Module</div><div class=\"flex justify-between\"><div class=\"p-4 flex flex-col justify-between\"><p class=\"font-bold line-clamp-1\">Teacher as Researcher: Try, Reflect, Share</p><p class=\"text-slate-600 line-clamp-2\">This module invites you to step into a shared cycle of teacher-research by teaching the Layered Writing lesson sequence, observing student thinking, and reflecting on what you notice across classrooms.</p><p class=\"text-slate-400 text-sm\">participate.community</p></div><img class=\"h-32 w-32 border-l border-slate-300 object-cover\" src=\"https://participate.community/img/k/public/87d1569-Pink%20Module%204.png\"></div></a></div><p></p><h2 class=\"text-4xl font-bold\" data-version=\"0\" id=\"h_-earn-recognition\">🏅 Earn Recognition</h2><p>As you work through the modules, you can earn digital credentials to recognize your progress and learning. For each module, you’ll automatically receive a <b>badge</b> when you participate in the discussion, where you’ll reflect on your learning and exchange ideas with other teachers. You also have the opportunity to earn a <b>microcredential</b> by submitting coursework for the module; your facilitator will review your work, provide individual feedback, and award the microcredential. Once you’ve earned all badges and microcredentials for the fall modules, you’ll automatically receive the <b>Sustaining Literacy Routines credential</b>, marking your full completion of the semester’s work.</p><div data-type=\"badge-embed\" data-badge-id=\"ee776d4d-e4c4-49da-a698-d35a3f5f2ce4\" data-badge-type=\"credential\"><a href=\"https://participate.community/badge/ee776d4d-e4c4-49da-a698-d35a3f5f2ce4\" class=\"flex flex-col border border-slate-300\"><div class=\"font-bold bg-slate-300 h-6 w-full pl-4\">Credential</div><div class=\"flex justify-between\"><div class=\"p-4 flex flex-col justify-between\"><p class=\"font-bold line-clamp-1\">Sustaining Literacy Routines</p><p class=\"text-slate-600 line-clamp-2\">This credential recognizes your full participation in the Literacy th@t Works spring online course modules. By completing all modules, earning each badge and microcredential, and engaging in reflection and discussion, you have demonstrated a sustained commitment to literacy routines and practicing teacher inquiry. This credential signifies your accomplishment in completing the spring semester coursework and your readiness to carry these practices forward into your classroom and future professional learning.</p><p class=\"text-slate-400 text-sm\">participate.community</p></div><img class=\"h-32 w-32 border-l border-slate-300 object-cover\" src=\"https://participate.community/img/k/public/4d5b827-Credential%20Sustaining%20Literacy.png\"></div></a></div><h2 class=\"text-4xl font-bold\" data-version=\"0\" id=\"h_spring-modules-checklist\">Spring Modules Checklist</h2><p>Click <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/18Z6KuG1Cu10igBwiYh994ie8jBML372P/view?usp=sharing\" class=\"underline\" target=\"_blank\"><span>here</span></a> to download a copy of the checklist.</p><iframe src=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/18Z6KuG1Cu10igBwiYh994ie8jBML372P/preview\" height=\"500\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" sandbox=\"allow-scripts allow-forms allow-same-origin allow-popups allow-popups-to-escape-sandbox\" title=\"Iframe for url: https://drive.google.com/file/d/18Z6KuG1Cu10igBwiYh994ie8jBML372P/preview\" style=\"width: 100%;\"></iframe><h2 class=\"text-4xl font-bold\" data-version=\"0\" id=\"h_-let-s-get-started\">➡️ Let's get started!</h2><div data-type=\"doc-embed\" data-doc-id=\"adebdcd4-d3c9-439b-bb5f-88cfd9a1b9df\" data-doc-type=\"module\"><a href=\"https://participate.community/docs/adebdcd4-d3c9-439b-bb5f-88cfd9a1b9df\" class=\"flex flex-col border border-slate-300\"><div class=\"font-bold bg-slate-300 h-6 w-full pl-4\">Module</div><div class=\"flex justify-between\"><div class=\"p-4 flex flex-col justify-between\"><p class=\"font-bold line-clamp-1\">Everyday Sparks 2.0: Deepening Routine Writing</p><p class=\"text-slate-600 line-clamp-2\">Building on the Everyday Sparks work from the fall, this module invites teachers to explore strategies for sustaining routine writing throughout the year while deepening students’ thinking and engagement.</p><p class=\"text-slate-400 text-sm\">participate.community</p></div><img class=\"h-32 w-32 border-l border-slate-300 object-cover\" src=\"https://participate.community/img/k/public/9c5e059-Pink%20Module%201.png\"></div></a></div>",
